       sscchheedd__yyiieelldd()  causes  the  calling  thread to relinquish the CPU.  The
       thread is moved to the end of the queue for its static priority  and  a
       new thread gets to run.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       On success, sscchheedd__yyiieelldd() returns 0.  On error, -1 is returned, and _e_r_‐
       _r_n_o is set to indicate the error.

EERRRROORRSS
       In the Linux implementation, sscchheedd__yyiieelldd() always succeeds.

