CCAAVVEEAATTSS
       sscchheedd__yyiieelldd() is intended for use with  real‐time  scheduling  policies
       (i.e., SSCCHHEEDD__FFIIFFOO or SSCCHHEEDD__RRRR).  Use of sscchheedd__yyiieelldd() with nondetermin‐
       istic  scheduling  policies such as SSCCHHEEDD__OOTTHHEERR is unspecified and very
       likely means your application design is broken.

       If the calling thread is the only thread in the highest  priority  list
       at that time, it will continue to run after a call to sscchheedd__yyiieelldd().

       Avoid  calling  sscchheedd__yyiieelldd()  unnecessarily  or inappropriately (e.g.,
       when resources needed by other schedulable threads are  still  held  by
       the  caller),  since  doing  so  will  result  in  unnecessary  context
       switches, which will degrade system performance.

